GUIDANCE

  Fred: "Change how the window move works so that Meta + right click
  and drag over an existing window and release on it splits that
  window. I had the following screen split: [A left half top one
  window] [B right half top and bottom one window] [C left bottom half
  left quarter] [D left bottom half right quater]. When I tried to drag
  D over B so that I'd have four equal windows on my screen I could not
  do it. Find the root cause and fix."

ROOT CAUSE

  The Tamlinux session binds Meta+mouse:273 to
  tp.dsp.mouse_move("tam-menu toggle start"), so the drag started a
  tiled move grab. On release, src/input/pointer.c only called
  tp_client_set_monitor(), which returns at once when the window stays
  on its monitor. Nothing looked at the window under the pointer, so
  dropping on the same monitor did nothing. A drop on another monitor
  put the window beside that monitor's last focused window, not the
  one under the pointer.

DONE

  - A tiled move released over another tiled window (found by tile
    geometry, so windows that draw less than their tile still count)
    removes the dragged window from the layout and inserts it beside
    the target. It splits the target's tile by the same rules as a new
    window: the W47 auto split with its 8 px centre band, or smart_split
    when that is on. Same and different monitors both work.
  - New tp_layout_drop(). Dwindle only; master, scroller and monocle
    return false and keep their old behaviour.
  - tp_dwindle_remove() now carries the parent's box to the sibling
    that replaces it, so dropping onto your own sibling splits the area
    it now owns, not its stale box.
  - Fred's A/B/C/D case is a unit test in test_layouts: D dropped on
    B's lower half gives four 960x540 quarters. test_input_headless
    drives the real Meta+drag path: a drop on itself changes nothing,
    a drop on another window splits it, and a second drop restores the
    layout.
  - make test passes: test_layouts 132, test_dwindle 151,
    test_input_headless 1089, smoke 6/6, test_visuals_gles2 73.
  - Version 0.4.5.

FAILED

  - The first headless check pressed at the window centre. The test
    clients draw 2x2 buffers, so the surface hit test missed. This led
    to finding the target by tile geometry.

